srow(352, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND DAVID BOUGHT THE THRESHING FLOOR AND THE OXEN FOR FIFTY SHEKELS OF SILVER" (2 Samuel 24:24), AND ELSEWHERE "DAVID GAVE ORNAN FOR THE PLACE SIX HUNDRED SHEKELS OF GOLD BY WEIGHT" (1 Chronicles 21:25) — NOT GOLD, FOR SILVER IS SAID; NOT SILVER, FOR GOLD IS SAID: HE BOUGHT WITH SILVER AND WEIGHED GOLD; NOT FIFTY, FOR SIX HUNDRED IS SAID; NOT SIX HUNDRED, FOR FIFTY IS SAID: WHEN DAVID SAW THE PLACE FIT FOR THE CHOSEN HOUSE HE COLLECTED FIFTY SHEKELS FROM EVERY TRIBE — SIX HUNDRED FROM ALL THE TRIBES. ({SP_(352, 13, "בכסף", "קנה", "וזהב", "שקל")} "with silver he bought and gold he weighed"; {SP_(352, 13, "עמד", "וכנס", "חמשים", "שקלים", "מכל", "שבט", "ושבט")} "he stood and collected fifty shekels from every tribe"): THE TWO PRICES RECONCILED — fifty times twelve = six hundred (the shelf\'s arithmetic on the Writings\' seats, cited never read; the translator: Sifrei Numbers 42 the twin, and this row unevenly attested); the row cites no verse of the chapter (one of the seven), read whole. The compile: no law — a DATA row of the shelf\'s reconciliation (twelve tribes the tape\'s count). DV33-05. Fresh.')
srow(352, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'WHY DID BENJAMIN MERIT THE SHEKHINAH IN HIS PORTION? A PARABLE OF A KING WHO VISITS HIS SONS AT TIMES, EACH SAYING "WITH ME HE STAYS"; THE YOUNGEST SAID: CAN FATHER LEAVE MY ELDER BROTHERS AND STAY WITH ME? AND STOOD WITH HIS FACE FALLEN AND HIS SOUL GRIEVED; THE KING: THE FOOD AND DRINK SHALL BE YOURS, MY LODGING WITH HIM — SO THE HOLY ONE: THE CHOSEN HOUSE IN BENJAMIN\'S PORTION, AND THE OFFERINGS FROM ALL THE TRIBES. ({SP_(352, 14, "בית", "הבחירה", "יהא", "בחלק", "בנימן", "וקרבנות", "מכל")} "the chosen house shall be in Benjamin\'s portion and the offerings from all"): THE FIRST REASON — the youngest\'s modesty; the offerings from all the tribes (Shekalim 1:1\'s half-shekel of all Israel the answer sheet\'s row, cited — the compile\'s case). The compile: no law. DV33-05. Fresh.')
srow(352, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: WHY DID BENJAMIN MERIT THE SHEKHINAH IN HIS PORTION? ALL THE TRIBES WERE BORN OUTSIDE THE LAND AND BENJAMIN WAS BORN IN THE LAND. ({SP_(352, 15, "שכל", "השבטים", "נולדו", "בחוצה", "לארץ", "ובנימן", "נולד")} "that all the tribes were born outside the land and Benjamin was born"): THE SECOND REASON — Benjamin\'s birth at Ephrath (Genesis 35:16-18 on the tape, a RUN CITATION; the tape\'s own entries answer: eleven sons born in Paddan-aram, the twelfth in Canaan). The compile: no law — a status the tape already holds by its birth entries. DV33-05. Fresh.')
srow(352, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: ALL THE TRIBES WERE IN THE SALE OF JOSEPH AND BENJAMIN WAS NOT; THE HOLY ONE SAID: IF I TELL THESE TO BUILD ME THE CHOSEN HOUSE, WHEN THEY PRAY BEFORE ME I WILL NOT BE FILLED WITH MERCY FOR THEM, FOR THEY HAD NO MERCY ON THEIR BROTHER. ({SP_(352, 16, "ובנימן", "לא", "היה", "במכירתו")} "and Benjamin was not in his sale"): THE THIRD REASON — Genesis 37:26-28\'s sale on the tape (a RUN CITATION; Benjamin absent from the brothers there — the tape\'s roster answers); the house of prayer built by the merciful. The compile: no law. DV33-05. Fresh.')
srow(352, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: WHY DID BENJAMIN MERIT THE SHEKHINAH IN HIS PORTION? A PARABLE OF A KING WITH MANY SONS: GROWN, EACH SEIZED HIS PLACE; THE YOUNGEST HIS FATHER LOVED, ATE AND DRANK WITH HIM, LEANED ON HIM GOING OUT AND COMING IN — SO BENJAMIN THE RIGHTEOUS, THE YOUNGEST OF THE TRIBES, JACOB ATE AND DRANK WITH HIM AND LEANED ON HIM; THE HOLY ONE SAID: THE PLACE WHERE THIS RIGHTEOUS ONE LAID HIS HANDS, THERE I SET MY SHEKHINAH — "AND BETWEEN HIS SHOULDERS HE DWELLS". ({SP_(352, 17, "מקום", "שסמך", "צדיק", "זה", "ידיו", "אני", "משרה")} "the place where this righteous one laid his hands, I set"): THE FOURTH REASON — the shoulders Benjamin\'s, leaned on by Jacob: the piska\'s last row closes on 33:12\'s last clause (the seat 33:12); the export\'s English "Dt.23:12" the misprint judged by the Hebrew. The compile: no law — the four reasons a status on the sanctuary\'s tribe (DV33-05). REREAD WHOLE (chapters 22-25\'s reading — the misprinted 23:12, excluded there; seated here at 33:12).')
srow(353, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND OF JOSEPH HE SAID: BLESSED OF THE LORD BE HIS LAND" (33:13) — IT TEACHES THAT JOSEPH\'S LAND IS BLESSED ABOVE ALL THE LANDS. ({SP_(353, 1, "מלמד", "שארצו", "של", "יוסף", "מברכת", "מכל", "הארצות")} "it teaches that Joseph\'s land is blessed above all the lands"): JOSEPH\'S LAND FIRST — the head row on 33:13 (the piska runs to 33:17 by its rows\' own markers). The compile: a status on Joseph\'s portion (reference). DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE PRECIOUS THINGS OF HEAVEN, FOR THE DEW" — THAT DEW BE FOUND IN IT EVERY HOUR; "AND FOR THE DEEP THAT COUCHES BENEATH" — IT TEACHES THAT IT MAKES THE SPRINGS COUCH. ({SP_(353, 2, "שיהא", "טל", "מצוי", "לה", "בכל", "שעה")} "that dew be found in it every hour"; {SP_(353, 2, "מלמד", "שהיא", "מרבצת", "מעינות")} "it teaches that it makes the springs couch"): THE DEW AND THE SPRINGS — "couches" (rovetzet) read as a causative (marbetzet, the springs bedded); Onkelos\'s "springs of fountains" (33:13\'s row) the same. The compile: no law. DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND FOR THE PRECIOUS THINGS OF THE FRUITS OF THE SUN" (33:14) — IT TELLS THAT JOSEPH\'S LAND IS OPEN TO THE SUN, AND NO FRUIT IS FAIR AND SWEET BUT THAT WHICH SEES THE SUN; AND AS IT IS OPEN TO THE SUN SO TO THE MOON — "THE PRECIOUS THINGS OF THE YIELD OF THE MOONS". ({SP_(353, 3, "מגיד", "שארצו", "של", "יוסף", "פתוחה", "לחמה")} "it tells that Joseph\'s land is open to the sun"; {SP_(353, 3, "כך", "פתוחה", "ללבנה")} "so it is open to the moon"): THE SUN AND THE MOON — the row seats at 33:14 by its marker (the seat rule by row); the fruit that sees the sun. The compile: no law. DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND FOR THE TOPS OF THE ANCIENT MOUNTAINS" (33:15) — IT TEACHES THAT JOSEPH\'S MOUNTAINS PRECEDE THE SANCTUARY\'S MOUNTAINS, AND THE SANCTUARY\'S MOUNTAINS PRECEDE THE MOUNTAINS OF THE LAND OF ISRAEL. ({SP_(353, 4, "מלמד", "שהררי", "יוסף", "קודמים", "להררי", "מקדש")} "it teaches that Joseph\'s mountains precede the sanctuary\'s mountains"): "ANCIENT" AS "PRECEDING" — kedem read as priority in creation (the sanctuary\'s mountains second, the land\'s third); Onkelos reads "early-ripening" (33:15\'s row). The compile: no law. DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND FOR THE PRECIOUS THINGS OF THE EVERLASTING HILLS" — IT TEACHES THAT THE FATHERS AND THE MOTHERS ARE CALLED MOUNTAINS AND HILLS: "I WILL GET ME TO THE MOUNTAIN OF MYRRH AND TO THE HILL OF FRANKINCENSE" (Song of Songs 4:6). ({SP_(353, 5, "מלמד", "שאבות", "ואמהות", "קרוים", "הרים", "וגבעות")} "it teaches that the fathers and the mothers are called mountains and hills"): THE PATRIARCHS AS HILLS — Genesis 49:26\'s "everlasting hills" (Jacob\'s own phrase for Joseph, the ink\'s kin) read here as the ancestors; the Song cited, never read. The compile: no law. DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND FOR THE PRECIOUS THINGS OF THE EARTH AND ITS FULNESS" (33:16) — IT TEACHES THAT JOSEPH\'S LAND IS FULL AND LACKS NO BLESSING; R. SHIMON BEN YOCHAI: A MAN MOORS HIS SHIP IN JOSEPH\'S PORTION AND NEEDS NOTHING FROM OUTSIDE IT. ({SP_(353, 6, "מלמד", "שארצו", "של", "יוסף", "מלאה", "ואינה", "חסרה")} "it teaches that Joseph\'s land is full and lacks"; {SP_(353, 6, "אדם", "מעמיד", "ספינתו", "בחלקו", "של", "יוסף")} "a man moors his ship in Joseph\'s portion"): THE FULL LAND — the ship that needs no port beyond (the coast of Ephraim and Manasseh — Joshua 16-17 cited, never read); the row seats at 33:16 by its marker. The compile: no law. DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE GOOD WILL OF HIM THAT DWELT IN THE BUSH" — FOR HE DID THE WILL OF HIM WHO WAS REVEALED TO MOSES IN THE BUSH. ({SP_(353, 7, "שעשה", "רצון", "מי", "שנגלה", "על", "משה", "בסנה")} "for he did the will of Him who was revealed to Moses in the bush"): THE BUSH — Exodus 3:2 on the tape (a RUN CITATION; Onkelos\'s "revealed to Moses in the bush" at 33:16 word for word with the Sifrei — the rendering and the homily one teaching); "good will" read as Joseph\'s doing of the will. The compile: no law. DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"LET IT COME UPON THE HEAD OF JOSEPH" — HE CAME AT THE HEAD TO EGYPT AND HE WILL COME AT THE HEAD IN THE TIME TO COME; "AND UPON THE CROWN OF HIM THAT WAS SEPARATE FROM HIS BRETHREN" — HIM WHOM HIS BRETHREN PUT FAR AND MADE A NAZIRITE. ({SP_(353, 8, "הוא", "בא", "בראש", "למצרים")} "he came at the head to Egypt"; {SP_(353, 8, "למי", "שרחקוהו", "אחיו", "ועשאוהו", "נזיר")} "to him whom his brothers put far and made a nazirite"): THE HEAD AND THE NAZIRITE — "head" read as first (Genesis 37:28\'s descent on the tape, the first of the brothers in Egypt — a RUN CITATION), "separate" (nazir) read as the nazirite\'s word (Numbers 6\'s compiled span cited — a homograph the shelf itself plays on: the crown\'s "separate" and the vow\'s "nazirite" one root); Genesis 49:26\'s line whole (the ink). The compile: the nazirite\'s word a FALSE edge for the census (named). DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"HIS FIRSTLING BULLOCK, MAJESTY IS HIS" (33:17) — IT TEACHES THAT MAJESTY (HOD) WAS GIVEN TO MOSES AND SPLENDOR (HADAR) TO JOSHUA; HAD MAJESTY BEEN GIVEN TO JOSHUA THE WORLD COULD NOT HAVE STOOD. ({SP_(353, 9, "מלמד", "שנתן", "לו", "הוד", "למשה", "והדר", "ליהושע")} "it teaches that majesty was given to Moses and splendor to Joshua"): THE BULLOCK IS JOSHUA — Ephraim\'s son (Numbers 13:8 on the tape); Numbers 27:20\'s "put of your majesty upon him" (the compiled succession, on the tape — a RUN CITATION: "of" your majesty, not all of it — the Sifrei\'s reading of the partitive) the seat that grounds the row; the row seats at 33:17 by its marker. The compile: a REFERENCE to the succession\'s runner (Joshua\'s status). DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HIS HORNS ARE THE HORNS OF THE WILD OX" — THE OX IS STRONG BUT ITS HORNS ARE NOT FAIR; THE WILD OX\'S HORNS ARE FAIR BUT IT IS NOT STRONG: JOSHUA WAS GIVEN THE OX\'S STRENGTH AND THE WILD OX\'S HORNS. ({SP_(353, 10, "נתן", "ליהושע", "כחו", "של", "שור", "וקרנו", "של")} "Joshua was given the strength of the ox and the horn of"): THE TWO BEASTS JOINED — Joshua the ox in strength, the wild ox in horns (Balaam\'s wild ox on the tape, Numbers 23:22). The compile: no law. DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITH THEM HE SHALL GORE THE PEOPLES" — DID JOSHUA CONQUER ALL THE PEOPLES? HE CONQUERED ONLY THIRTY-ONE KINGS! IT TEACHES THAT HE CONQUERED KINGS AND RULERS FROM ONE END OF THE WORLD TO THE OTHER. ({SP_(353, 11, "והלא", "לא", "כבש", "אלא", "שלשים", "ואחד", "מלכים")} "did he not conquer only thirty-one kings"): THE THIRTY-ONE — Joshua 12:9-24\'s list (cited, never read; the number the shelf\'s, not the ink\'s — no count owed by the compile); the goring verb (the ox\'s law\'s homograph, 33:17\'s Onkelos row) read as conquest. The compile: no law. DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"TOGETHER, THE ENDS OF THE EARTH" — DID JOSHUA CONQUER ALL THE LANDS? ONLY THIS SMALL PART! BUT ALL THE KINGS HE SUBDUED WERE KINGS AND RULERS; R. YEHUDA: WERE THE THIRTY-ONE KINGS ALL IN THE LAND OF ISRAEL? AS THEY DO IN ROME NOW — EVERY KING AND RULER WHO HAS NOT BOUGHT PALACES AND VILLAS IN ROME SAYS "I HAVE DONE NOTHING", SO EVERY KING AND RULER WHO HAD NOT BOUGHT PALACES AND VILLAS IN THE LAND SAID "I HAVE DONE NOTHING". ({SP_(353, 12, "והלא", "לא", "כבש", "אלא", "פרטוס", "זה", "קטן")} "did he not conquer only this small part"; {SP_(353, 12, "כדרך", "שעושים", "ברומי", "עכשיו")} "as they do in Rome now"): THE KINGS\' VILLAS — R. Yehuda\'s answer to the thirty-one (foreign kings holding estates in the land; the translator\'s twin 37:8, read at chapters 1-3); Rome named as the present. The compile: no law. DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(353, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"THEY ARE THE TEN THOUSANDS OF EPHRAIM" — SINCE THE CANAANITES\' WEALTH IS NOT TOLD US: "ADONI-BEZEK SAID: SEVENTY KINGS WITH THUMBS AND TOES CUT OFF GATHERED UNDER MY TABLE" (Judges 1:7) — AN ARGUMENT FROM THE LESSER: IF ADONI-BEZEK, NOT FIT TO BE COUNTED AMONG CANAAN\'S KINGS, HAD SEVENTY KINGS UNDER HIS TABLE, LEARN THE CANAANITES\' WEALTH; "THEY ARE THE THOUSANDS OF MANASSEH" — SINCE IT IS NOT TOLD HOW MANY CANAANITES JOSHUA KILLED: "ZEBAH AND ZALMUNNA IN KARKOR AND THEIR HOSTS ABOUT FIFTEEN THOUSAND, ALL THAT WERE LEFT … AND THERE FELL A HUNDRED AND TWENTY THOUSAND" (Judges 8:10) — A HUNDRED AND THIRTY-FIVE THOUSAND, TO FULFILL "THE TEN THOUSANDS OF EPHRAIM AND THE THOUSANDS OF MANASSEH". ({SP_(353, 13, "לפי", "שלא", "מפרש", "לנו", "עשרם", "של", "כנעניים")} "since the wealth of the Canaanites is not told us"; {SP_(353, 13, "הרי", "מאה", "ושלשים", "וחמשה", "אלף")} "that is a hundred and thirty-five thousand"): THE MYRIADS AND THE THOUSANDS COUNTED FROM JUDGES — the a-fortiori (qal vachomer, I1) from Adoni-bezek\'s seventy, and the sum 15,000 + 120,000 (the shelf\'s arithmetic on the Prophets\' seats, cited never read — Gideon\'s war, not Joshua\'s, the translator leaves as is); the ink\'s construct plurals read as counts by the Sifrei — no number line from the ink (the parser\'s silence), the shelf\'s numbers DATA. The compile: no law. DV33-06. Fresh.')
srow(354, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND OF ZEBULUN HE SAID" (33:18) — WHY? BECAUSE "FROM AMONG HIS BRETHREN HE TOOK FIVE MEN AND PRESENTED THEM TO PHARAOH" (Genesis 47:2) AND THEIR NAMES WERE NOT GIVEN — THIS IS ONE OF THEM. ({SP_(354, 1, "ולא", "נתפרשו", "שמותם", "וזה", "אחד", "מהם")} "and their names were not given, and this is one of them"): THE FIVE BEFORE PHARAOH — Genesis 47:2 on the tape (a RUN CITATION; the five unnamed there named by the Sifrei from the blessing\'s framed tribes: the translator sends to 355:1-7 for the rest — RUN 4); the head row on 33:18. The compile: a status on Zebulun (reference). DV33-07. Fresh.')
srow(354, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"REJOICE, ZEBULUN, IN YOUR GOING OUT" — IT TEACHES THAT ZEBULUN WAS A BROKER FOR HIS BRETHREN, BUYING FROM HIS BRETHREN AND SELLING TO THE NATIONS, AND FROM THE NATIONS TO HIS BRETHREN. ({SP_(354, 2, "מלמד", "שהיה", "זבולן", "סרסור", "לאחיו")} "it teaches that Zebulun was a broker for his brothers"): THE MERCHANT — the going out read as trade (Genesis 49:13\'s haven of ships on the tape — Jacob\'s word; the ink: the two blessings share Zebulun\'s name alone); Onkelos reads war (33:18\'s row) — two readings, no law. DV33-07. Fresh.')
srow(354, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ISSACHAR IN YOUR TENTS" — IT TEACHES THAT THE TRIBE OF ISSACHAR IS PRAISED IN TORAH: "OF THE CHILDREN OF ISSACHAR, MEN THAT HAD UNDERSTANDING OF THE TIMES" (1 Chronicles 12:33); AND SO HIS FATHER PRAISED HIM: "AND HE SAW THAT REST WAS GOOD" (Genesis 49:15). ({SP_(354, 3, "מלמד", "ששבטו", "של", "יששכר", "משתבח", "בתורה")} "it teaches that the tribe of Issachar is praised in Torah"): ISSACHAR\'S TORAH — the tents the study house; 1 Chronicles 12:33 the seat Onkelos\'s "times of the festivals" (33:18) draws on (cited, never read); Genesis 49:15 on the tape (a RUN CITATION). The compile: no law. DV33-07. Fresh.')
srow(354, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND ISSACHAR IN YOUR TENTS" — IT TEACHES THAT THE CHOSEN HOUSE WAS FIT TO BE BUILT IN ISSACHAR\'S PORTION. ({SP_(354, 4, "מלמד", "שבית", "הבחירה", "היה", "ראוי", "להבנות", "בחלקו")} "it teaches that the chosen house was fit to be built in the portion of"): A SECOND TRIBE FIT FOR THE HOUSE — Issachar\'s tents the sanctuary\'s might-have-been (352:10\'s dispute the actual); "fit" (ra\'ui), not built. The compile: no law. DV33-07. Fresh.')
srow(354, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"THEY SHALL CALL PEOPLES TO THE MOUNTAIN" (33:19) — WHENCE THAT NATIONS AND KINGDOMS GATHERED AND CAME TO THE MERCHANDISE OF THE LAND OF ISRAEL, SAYING: SINCE WE HAVE TROUBLED TO COME, LET US SEE WHAT THE JEWS\' MERCHANDISE IS — THEY GO UP TO JERUSALEM AND SEE ISRAEL SERVING ONE GOD AND EATING ONE FOOD (AMONG THE NATIONS THE GOD OF ONE IS NOT THE GOD OF ANOTHER, NOR THE FOOD), AND SAY: IT IS GOOD TO CLEAVE ONLY TO THIS NATION; WHENCE THAT THEY DO NOT MOVE FROM THERE UNTIL THEY CONVERT AND OFFER SACRIFICES AND BURNT OFFERINGS? "THERE THEY SHALL OFFER SACRIFICES OF RIGHTEOUSNESS". ({SP_(354, 5, "שהיו", "אמות", "ומלכיות", "מתכנסות", "ובאות", "לפרגמטיא", "של")} "that nations and kingdoms gathered and came to the merchandise of"; {SP_(354, 5, "שאין", "זזים", "משם", "עד", "שמתגירים")} "that they do not move from there until they convert"): THE PEOPLES CALLED ARE CONVERTS — the mountain Jerusalem (Onkelos\'s sanctuary mount at 33:19), the one God and the one food the draw, the sacrifices the converts\' (the proselyte\'s offering — Keritot 2:1\'s row the answer sheet\'s, cited, the compile\'s case); the row seats at 33:19 by its marker. The compile: a status on conversion by the sanctuary (reference; the proselyte a compiled status — Exodus 12:48 on the tape). DV33-07. Fresh.')
srow(354, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THEY SHALL SUCK THE ABUNDANCE OF THE SEAS" — TWO TAKE IN ABUNDANCE AND GIVE IN ABUNDANCE: THE SEA AND THE KINGDOM; THE SEA GIVES IN ABUNDANCE AND TAKES IN ABUNDANCE, THE KINGDOM GIVES IN ABUNDANCE AND TAKES IN ABUNDANCE. ({SP_(354, 6, "שנים", "נוטלים", "בשפע", "ונותנים", "בשפע")} "two take in abundance and give in abundance"; {SP_(354, 6, "ים", "ומלכות")} "the sea and the kingdom"): THE SEA AND THE STATE — the abundance\'s two givers and takers (the translator: fish and drownings, works and taxes). The compile: no law. DV33-07. Fresh.')
srow(354, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "THE ABUNDANCE OF THE SEAS" — THIS IS THE SEA OF HAIFA, STORED FOR THE RIGHTEOUS IN THE TIME TO COME: NO SHIP IS LOST IN THE GREAT SEA WITH ITS BUNDLE OF SILVER, GOLD, PRECIOUS STONES, PEARLS, GLASS AND EVERY PRECIOUS VESSEL BUT THE GREAT SEA SPEWS IT INTO THE SEA OF HAIFA, STORED FOR THE RIGHTEOUS — "THE ABUNDANCE OF THE SEAS"; R. YOSE: ONCE I WAS GOING FROM CHEZIB TO TYRE AND FOUND AN OLD MAN — YOUR LIVELIHOOD? — FROM THE CHILAZON — IS IT FOUND? — BY HEAVEN, THERE IS A PLACE IN THE SEA LYING AMONG MOUNTAINS, RINGED BY POISONOUS LIZARDS; NO MAN GOES THERE WHOM THEY DO NOT BITE, AND HE DIES AND ROTS IN HIS PLACE — I SAID: IT IS PLAIN THAT IT IS STORED FOR THE RIGHTEOUS. ({SP_(354, 7, "זה", "ימה", "של", "חיפה", "שגנוז", "לצדיקים", "לעתיד")} "this is the sea of Haifa, stored for the righteous for the future"; {SP_(354, 7, "אמר", "לי", "מחלזון")} "he said to me: from the chilazon"): THE BAY OF HAIFA AND THE CHILAZON — the sea\'s treasure for the righteous, and the blue dye\'s snail (Numbers 15:38\'s blue thread on the tape — the compiled fringe cited; the translator sends to Sifrei Numbers 115); R. Yose\'s road from Chezib to Tyre. The compile: no law — a DATA row on the snail\'s source (a parameter of the blue). DV33-07. Fresh.')
srow(354, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE HIDDEN TREASURES OF THE SAND" — "TREASURES": THE CHILAZON; "HIDDEN": THE TUNNY; "SAND": GLASS; BECAUSE THE TRIBE OF ZEBULUN COMPLAINED BEFORE THE PLACE: MASTER OF THE WORLD, TO MY BRETHREN YOU GAVE LANDS AND TO ME SEAS, TO MY BRETHREN FIELDS AND VINEYARDS AND TO ME THE CHILAZON! — IN THE END I WILL MAKE THEM NEED YOUR HAND FOR THIS CHILAZON; — WHO WILL TELL ME? — A SIGN IN YOUR HAND: WHOEVER STEALS FROM YOU WILL HAVE NOTHING IN HIS MERCHANDISE. ({SP_(354, 8, "ספני", "זו", "חלזון", "טמוני", "זו", "טרית", "חול")} "treasures — the chilazon; hidden — the tunny; sand"; {SP_(354, 8, "לאחי", "נתת", "ארצות", "ולי", "נתת", "ימים")} "to my brothers You gave lands and to me You gave seas"): THE THREE WORDS THREE WARES — the snail, the fish and the glass of Zebulun\'s coast; Zebulun\'s complaint answered by the blue thread\'s need (Numbers 15:38 on the tape); the piska\'s last row. The compile: no law. DV33-07. Fresh.')
